<title>CANADA: AT&amp;T Canada Long Distance names new chairman.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T Canada Long Distance names new chairman.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Canada Long Distance Services Co, Canada's second biggest long-distance telephone carrier, said on Thursday it named Barbara McDougall as chairman.</p>
<p>McDougall is a former Canadian cabinet minister, whose posts included foreign affairs and employment and immigration.</p>
<p>AT&amp;T Canada Long Distance is jointly owned by AT&amp;T Corp, Bank of Nova Scotia, Toronto-Dominion Bank and Royal Bank of Canada.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
</text>
